{#- RB4011 — HD-1097 DHCP option 15 (search suffix = {{ domain_local }}) DELTA, 2026-10-07.
    Why: `\\nas\media` is typed with a BARE host name. The LAN zone answered service names
    only (nas.kogler.si → NXDOMAIN, aa flag, on both home resolvers), so the mount rode the
    LLMNR/NetBIOS broadcast fallback — which a wired switch port supplies and a Wi-Fi client
    does not. Measured on the owner's laptop: mounting by IP over Wi-Fi works, by name it does
    not. Same change set: the host A records in `zone_kogler_si` (group_vars/all) answer the
    FQDN; THIS delta delivers option 15 so the bare name is devolved to the FQDN in the first
    place. One without the other leaves the bug half-fixed.
    Folded back into rb4011_converge.rsc.j2 + roles/router in the SAME change — a delta is
    transient and must never become a second truth (docs/network-ops.md §The three tiers).
    Idempotent: set-only (no add/remove), touches one property on the server rows; re-import
    of an already-correct value is a no-op. Reaches clients at their next ACK/renewal. -#}
# =============================================================================
# HD-1097 — set domain (DHCP option 15) on EVERY dhcp-server, dhcp-mgmt included
# =============================================================================
:local dom "{{ domain_local }}"
:foreach s in=[/ip dhcp-server find] do={
    :local n [/ip dhcp-server get $s name]
    /ip dhcp-server set $s domain=$dom
    :put ("HD-1097: " . $n . " -> domain=" . [/ip dhcp-server get $s domain])
}

# The `:foreach ... get` form is deliberate: over non-interactive SSH
# `/ip dhcp-server network print where ...` and `print as-value` print NOTHING and a bare
# `[find …]` resolves against the current menu, so both read as "not set" while the value is
# set (measured 2026-10-07, HD-1095). Read back with get, never with a filtered print.
#
# Verify (device):  /ip dhcp-server print detail      → every row shows domain=kogler.si
# Verify (client):  Windows: ipconfig /all → "Connection-specific DNS Suffix . : kogler.si"
#                   then:  Resolve-DnsName nas.kogler.si  → 10.10.1.10
